## EGL vendor resolution verified inside the container
Tested via dlopen of libEGL.so.1 (no headers in image):
  WITH    __EGL_VENDOR_LIBRARY_FILENAMES=/usr/share/glvnd/egl_vendor.d/10_nvidia.json
          eglInitialize=1, EGL 1.5, EGL_VENDOR = "NVIDIA"      <- CORRECT
  WITHOUT the pin (variable emptied)
          eglInitialize=0                                    <- FAILS
This confirms the unit's documented reason for the pin: Mesa's dri2 platform
claims the NVIDIA render node and EGL cannot initialise. Pin is retained.

## Gazebo GUI faults diagnosed this session
1. FIXED - gz-transport discovery. Server runs GZ_IP=127.0.0.1, GUI did not.
   Symptom: "[GUI] GUI requesting list of world names" every 5s forever, black
   viewport, server healthy in the same network namespace.
   Fix: Environment=GZ_IP=127.0.0.1 added to ao-sim-fabrication-gui-gz.container
   (both repo and ~/.config/containers/systemd/) and to ao-sim-gui-client.sh.
   After fix the client reaches the world: ogre2 plugin loads and
   "Camera pose topic advertised on [/gui/camera/pose]".
2. OPEN - abort ~0.94s after camera pose advertises (first rendered frame):
     terminate called after throwing 'std::logic_error'
     what(): basic_string: construction from null is not valid
   thrown from a Qt event handler (thread 72, libQt6Core frame).
   Offscreen probe (QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen) ran 55s+ WITHOUT crashing, so the
   fault is on the real GL/XCB path, not QML and not discovery.
   Coredumps: ulimit -c unlimited added to launcher, but container processes do
   not reach host systemd-coredump (0 entries for gz-sim). Stack not yet obtained.
   Ruled out: GZ_SIM_SERVER_CONFIG_PATH / GZ_SIM_RENDER_ENGINE_PATH (unset on the
   GUI but also unset on the server, which runs fine).
   Material spam "Can't assign material scene::Material(N)" x1210 is cosmetic;
   gazebo.material lives at /usr/share/gz/gz-sim/media/ which ogre2 does not load.

